  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056271/assets/61ed37aa6a5e67cdc60cca2c93969a47d12e1e36f18edf96f646922877641e79.png)\n\nThe vector $u$ is an eigenvector of a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\frac{1}{2}.$ Find the vector $Au.$",
  "worked_solution": "The eigenvector $u=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =\\frac{1}{2}.$ So, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Au & =\\frac{1}{2}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we have the following picture:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056271/assets/c272ff1454ac4ab9825e312f563c9bca08ac2800faa0e95ab45e8a5e827369da.png)",
